summary: |-
  Atelier session .atelier/sessions/2026-10-20-gnomon-mod-invitations, with comps refs/boards.html and refs/flow.html (day/night, reduced motion).
  Recommendations:
  (1) Invitation = a margin slip under the reply that offered: dashed, soft shadow, never key-styled; a GUI-drawn tab `offer · mod:<name>` plus a manifest "takes:" line; only the question is model text; Open (trusted click/↵) and "not now". Rejected: a Workshop cap walk (nagging), composer suggestions (next to kernel cards).
  (2) Handoff = a companion leaf beside the chat inside the centre column only; a `↳ handed to mod:<name>` row; esc folds to an edge tab; "done" returns. A ⤢ sheet is optional; headless mods work through the cap.
  (3) Results = a returned sheet labelled `↳ tool output · mod:<name>`, then synthesis prose and at most ONE next slip; a trail line `constellation ✓ → neurons ?`. Rejected: a tray of next steps (nagging).
  (4) Local UI = a framed world: the GUI-owned fence (tab, hatched gutter, project-hue top edge); first-party mods may declare world: sky|loom (the GUI applies its palette; mods never ship CSS); identity = glyph plus name, no per-mod hue.
  Aligns with Arky's design.
  Luna's 4 founder questions (voice "open" path, mod identity, worlds, "not now" duration) plus Arky's 10 are pending.
  Aegis calls: buttons inside the leaf/sheet (centre column, away from decision keys) and voice accept.
